<title>UK: IRAQ SAYS PUMPED 710,000 BPD OF CRUDE IN JULY.</title>
<headline>IRAQ SAYS PUMPED 710,000 BPD OF CRUDE IN JULY.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>Iraq told OPEC it pumped 710,000 barrels a day (bpd) of crude in July, OPEC news agency reported on Monday.</p>
<p>Baghdad supplied the data to OPEC secretariat headquarters in Vienna.</p>
<p>Delays to the second phase of the United Nations oil-for-food exchange with Baghdad meant Iraq was restricted to production for domestic needs and sales to Jordan in July.</p>
<p>Supply as defined by OPEC is calculated as domestic consumption plus net export sales of crude and products, plus withdrawals of stocks held outside national boundaries.</p>
<p>Production and supply data for July according to member country submissions to the OPEC Secretariat were as follows (in million bpd):  </p>
<p>			Production     Supply</p>
<p>     Algeria	  0.8020	 0.8000</p>
<p>     Indonesia	1.3269	 n/a</p>
<p>     Iran</p>
<p>     Iraq	     0.710	  0.7100</p>
<p>     Kuwait	   2.0081	 2.0068</p>
<p>     Libya	    1.3910	 1.3900</p>
<p>     Nigeria</p>
<p>     Qatar	    0.3912	 0.3571</p>
<p>     Saudi Arabia   8.0003	 8.0007</p>
<p>     UAE		2.1153	 2.1609</p>
<p>     Venezuela	2.4130	 n/a</p>
</text>
